---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Hypothesis & Parallel Test — The Green Screen"
  description="An empirical experiment testing whether narrative makes green retrofitting more emotionally legible than technical data alone."
>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b-2 border-ink pb-6 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-rust mb-1">Scientific Rigour & Empirical Inquiry</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink">The Parallel Reader Test</h1>
      <blockquote class="font-display italic text-lg text-ink-60 mt-3 leading-relaxed border-l-2 border-forest pl-4">
        "If people encounter green retrofit through narrative (such as a story about a specific building and its people) they will be more likely to support or adopt retrofit measures than if they encounter it through technical information alone."
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <!-- The Problem & Solution Breakdown as specified in the brief -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
      <div class="border border-ink-12 p-6 space-y-3 bg-canvas">
        <p class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-rust font-semibold">The Problem</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Socially Stalled</h2>
        <p class="font-ui text-[13px] text-ink-60 leading-relaxed">
          Green retrofitting is technically solvable but socially stalled. The people who inhabit buildings experience retrofitting as disruption, displacement, or expense, not as climate action. Engineering, while a popular solution, reveals that the gap is narrative.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border border-ink-12 p-6 space-y-3 bg-canvas">
        <p class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-forest font-semibold">The Solution</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Emotionally Legible</h2>
        <p class="font-ui text-[13px] text-ink-60 leading-relaxed">
          The Green Screen uses climate fiction to make green retrofitting emotionally legible. The story creates the emotional entry point. The Atlas provides the technical substance. The Screening Room turns readers into a community through recorded readings and conversations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The Test Design -->
    <div class="border-2 border-ink p-8 space-y-6 bg-canvas mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-ink-12 pb-3">
        <p class="font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-60">Methodology & Research Protocol</p>
        <span class="font-mono text-[9px] px-2 py-0.5 border border-forest text-forest uppercase font-semibold">Study Design</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The Test Protocol</h3>
        <p class="font-ui text-[13px] text-ink leading-relaxed">
          Create two parallel versions of one retrofit case study:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="border border-ink-12 p-4 space-y-1">
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-rust block font-semibold">Condition A</span>
            <h4 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink">Technical Brief</h4>
            <p class="font-ui text-[12px] text-ink-60">Data, costs, engineering specifications, and energy savings.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-ink-12 p-4 space-y-1">
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase text-forest block font-semibold">Condition B</span>
            <h4 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink">Short Story</h4>
            <p class="font-ui text-[12px] text-ink-60">Narrative fiction set in the building, focusing on inhabitants.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="font-ui text-[13px] text-ink-60 pt-2">
          Survey two groups of readers. Measure attitude shift, recall, and willingness to support retrofit policies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
